.Dd August 1, 2026
.Dt INTEGRIS-EVIDENCE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm integris-evidence
.Nd run Integris kernel evidence campaigns
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl root Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs kernel test campaigns for Integris reference packages and writes evidence
manifests under the
.Pa evidence/
tree (one subdirectory per campaign area) together with sibling
.Pa .sha256
digest files.
.Pp
A written campaign file is an artifact only.
Promoting
.Pa assurance/evidence.json
entries to status
.Dq produced
remains a separate review step.
.Nm
is assurance tooling, not a replication daemon.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width "-root dir"
.It Fl root Ar dir
Repository root (default:
.Pa . ) .
Must be a git checkout so
.Xr git 1
can resolve
.Li HEAD .
.El
.Ss Operation
For each configured campaign,
.Nm :
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
Invokes
.Xr go 1
tests (and selected short fuzz runs) with
.Ev GOTOOLCHAIN
forced to
.Li local .
.It
Captures command lines, exit codes, stdout tails, and SHA-256 digests.
.It
Records Go version, platform, source revision, residual gaps, and writes JSON
plus a matching
.Pa .sha256
sidecar.
.El
.Pp
Host tools required:
.Xr git 1
and
.Xr go 1
matching the pinned toolchain in
.Pa go.mod .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "evidence/*/*-campaign.json.sha256" -compact
.It Pa evidence/*/*-campaign.json
Campaign manifests.
.It Pa evidence/*/*-campaign.json.sha256
Digests of the JSON bodies.
.It Pa assurance/evidence.json
Registry of planned or produced evidence (not rewritten by this tool).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
All campaigns completed and manifests were written.
.It 1
Repository, tool, test, or I/O failure.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
integris-evidence -root .
make evidence
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr go 1 ,
.Xr integris-assure 1 ,
.Xr integris-release-digest 1 ,
.Xr integris 7
.Sh HISTORY
Introduced to produce machine-checkable kernel campaign artifacts during M1.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Integris contributors
.Sh CAVEATS
Non-zero subprocess exits fail the tool.
Residual gaps listed in manifests remain open until independent review closes
the corresponding verification records.
